From f1c60f8f53b17cbeb6e09deead906310cb11fe6b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: stephan-xyz <stephan@zehrer.xyz>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 08:16:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] netstack: watchdog that names the call a stuck main loop is
 in

netstack runs on one thread: one call that never returns stops the whole
stack, its netcfg scheme too (redox-rpi #92). The main loop now records
which event it handles and whether it is writing to or reading from the
network device. A second thread writes to /scheme/debug when that has
taken more than 5 s, again every 30 s, and once more when the loop comes
back.

The loop re-arms its timer at least every 500 ms. When no timer event has
come for 10 s and the loop is not stuck in a call, the thread writes that
as well, since then the loop waits for events that do not come. Every
10 min it writes a heartbeat with the stage and counts of events and
received frames, so a watchdog that does not run shows too.
---
 netstack/src/link/ethernet.rs |  13 ++-
 netstack/src/main.rs          |  23 +++-
 netstack/src/watch.rs         | 214 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 247 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 netstack/src/watch.rs

